<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Italy (Napoleonic)</h1><p class="st-meta">1805 CE – 1814 CE · capital Milan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Napoleon's Kingdom of Italy, ruled from Milan by his stepson Eugène de Beauharnais, which gave northern Italians a modern state and a common army.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> became emperor of the French, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/italian-republic-1802-1805">Italian Republic</a> (1802–1805) was turned into a kingdom. On 26 May 1805 Napoleon crowned himself king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan-cathedral">Milan Cathedral</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-crown-of-lombardy">Iron Crown of Lombardy</a>, and appointed his stepson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugene-de-beauharnais">Eugène de Beauharnais</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom grew to include <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a> in 1806, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marche</a> in 1808 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-tyrol">South Tyrol</a> in 1810, and for a time <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/histria">Istria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>, which passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/illyrian-provinces">Illyrian Provinces</a> in 1809. It had <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">departments</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prefect">prefects</a> on the French model, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-code">Napoleonic Code</a>, public schools and an efficient tax system. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conscription">conscript</a> army fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, where tens of thousands died in 1812.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon's</a> defeats, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugene-de-beauharnais">Eugène</a> signed an armistice in April 1814. A riot in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Milan</a> killed the finance minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-prina">Giuseppe Prina</a>, and Austrian troops took over; the territory became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-lombardy-venetia">Kingdom of Lombardy-Venetia</a> and other restored states.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-italy-napoleonic.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Italy (Napoleonic)" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Napoleonic_Kingdom_of_Italy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1805 CE – 1814 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Milan</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Napoleon Bonaparte, Eugène de Beauharnais</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>, <a href="/countries/slovenia">Slovenia</a>, <a href="/countries/croatia">Croatia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Regno d Italia (1805–1814), Napoleonic Kingdom of Italy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=kingdom-of-italy-napoleonic" aria-label="Kingdom of Italy (Napoleonic) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4898 574 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Italy (Napoleonic) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5218 830L5303 923M5218 830L5054 728M5218 830L5218 830"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5303 923h0M5054 728h0M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5218 830h0"/></svg></a>